<title>USA: Fannie Mae increases REMIC 1996-66 to $260 mln.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae increases REMIC 1996-66 to $260 mln.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal National Mortgage Association (Fannie Mae or FNMA) said it increased the size of a previous issue of Real Estate Mortgage Investment Conduit (REMIC) securities.</p>
<p>REMIC Trust 1996-66, through Merrill Lynch &amp; Co Inc, has been increased to approximately $260 million from $250 million, Fannie Mae said.</p>
<p>The issue is backed by 30-year 7.0 percent mortgage-backed securities and a FNMA REMIC tranche, FNMA said.</p>
<p>REMIC 1996-66 has a split settlement date of $250 million on December 17, and $10 million on December 27.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
